Totals grouped by language (dominant language first):
ansic:       197593 (95.35%)
cpp:           7083 (3.42%)
yacc:          2005 (0.97%)
lex:            377 (0.18%)
awk:             89 (0.04%)
sh:              70 (0.03%)
sed:             11 (0.01%)

Total Physical Source Lines of Code (SLOC)                = 207,228

Although LOC isn't a particularly good metric for determining the effort
to develop something, and a rewrite in a different language would have
different characteristics, you can at least get a sense of the scale of
the job.  My gut feeling is that, assuming that you've got several
people working on it regularly, but on their free time, that you're
probably still looking at multiple years of work.  Nethack's game logic
is quite complex, and implementing it will not be easy, regardless of
which language you use.

I would certainly hesitate to lend my time to such a project, when the
end result is going to be functionally identical to a program that
already exists.  If I was going to spend years on a roguelike game,
I would probably want to work on creating something new.

